---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/browse-abandonment';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/browse-abandonment');
const desc = "Turn permitted product-view data into relevant help without confusing a view, a cart addition and a checkout event.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is browse abandonment the same as cart recovery?",
    "answer": "No. A view signals research, an add-to-cart event creates a cart, and checkout start is another step. Use explicit event definitions and handoffs."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should every repeat view get a discount?",
    "answer": "No. Repeated research can reflect fit, delivery or trust questions. Decide whether an incentive is warranted using margin constraints and measured incremental response."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can anonymous visitors receive browse emails?",
    "answer": "A product view alone supplies neither a verified email identity nor permission. Enroll only when your identity and messaging eligibility rules are satisfied."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Shopify operating playbook</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Browse abandonment: useful follow-up for research intent</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Turn permitted product-view data into relevant help without confusing a view, a cart addition and a checkout event.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Define the event and eligible identity</h2>
      <p>A product view is a research signal, not a purchase commitment. Cart addition and checkout start are separate events; a cart abandoner has not necessarily started checkout. Preserve that distinction in trigger definitions and reporting.</p>
      <p>Record event ID, occurrence time, ingestion time, product or collection identifier and a legitimately resolved subscriber identity. A browser cookie or product view is not by itself permission to email. Do not guess an address for anonymous traffic or transfer one household member’s behavior to another profile.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Check tracking quality before setting thresholds</h2>
      <p>Exclude preview activity, repeated retries and obvious automation from the behavioral signals used to enroll recipients. Inspect duplicate views from page reloads and delayed events from earlier sessions. Time on page is useful only if the integration measures it reliably; a page-open event does not prove active reading.</p>
      <p>Choose candidate thresholds using observed consideration paths: repeat product visits, related collection exploration or a relevant guide visit. Specify a lookback window and event deduplication rule. More views do not automatically justify a discount, and fixed view counts do not fit every catalog.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose the product or collection deliberately</h2>
      <p>When several products were viewed, define whether the candidate uses the most recent eligible item, repeated interest or a collection story. Store the selection reason. Do not let an old delayed event replace a newer candidate simply because it arrived last.</p>
      <p>A room project may need a home-goods collection guide, while a ring setting needs material or sizing information. Version collection mappings when merchandising reorganizes the catalog. Apply an expiry to inferred interests so old research does not become a permanent customer preference.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Let stronger intent replace browse follow-up</h2>
      <p>An add-to-cart event should cancel the pending browse message for that purchase path and hand ownership to <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">cart recovery</a>. An order should invalidate an irrelevant reminder for the bought item. Recheck these states at dispatch, not just enrollment.</p>
      <p>Handle late purchase events and cross-device identity merges explicitly. An unrelated purchase need not cancel all research help, but suppress any offer that conflicts with the new order or active cart. Welcome and campaign sends also consume the subscriber’s contact budget.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Answer the research question in the creative</h2>
      <p>Use an accurate product recap, a useful differentiator and a clear path to the relevant information. For jewelry, consider sizing, warranty or an appointment; for pet products, fit or ingredient information; for furniture, dimensions and delivery constraints. Use genuine, appropriately matched reviews and supported claims.</p>
      <p>Avoid wording that exposes an exact browsing timestamp or implies certainty about private intent. A collection guide can be more useful than a grid of unrelated items. The <a class="link" href="/use-cases/email-design">design workflow</a> should verify product images, variant links, accessibility and mobile rendering.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose delays and stop conditions from evidence</h2>
      <p>Compare the time from research to cart and order in your own catalog. Select a first-message delay that allows ordinary shopping to finish, then test a relevant follow-up against a suitable comparison. High price is context for a considered journey, not a universal hours-to-send rule.</p>
      <p>Set candidate expiry, re-entry and total-contact rules. A new view need not restart a full sequence. Stop when interest becomes stale, permission changes, the product becomes irrelevant or the next message adds no value. A fixed three-touch series is not a requirement.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Make availability and offers separate decisions</h2>
      <p>Recheck product status, price and market availability before preparing the send. If unavailable, offer a permitted <a class="link" href="/use-cases/back-in-stock">waitlist</a> path or an explicitly labeled alternative. Do not send a purchase reminder to a deleted product or pretend a different size fulfills the viewed variant.</p>
      <p>Start with useful information where the unresolved question is fit, trust or suitability. An incentive needs an approved margin budget and terms coordinated with cart, welcome and campaigns. Consult <a class="link" href="/use-cases/discount-strategy">discount strategy</a>; repeated browsing alone does not establish price sensitivity.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Measure the whole intent path</h2>
      <p>Track unique eligible browsers, enrolled recipients, dispatched messages, cart additions and orders using explicit time windows. Report identified and anonymous coverage separately. A rise in identified browse events after tracking changes is not automatically a rise in demand.</p>
      <p>Measure net contribution and full-price mix alongside attributed orders. Revenue already net of discounts should not lose the discount a second time in margin calculations. Use a preplanned randomized comparison where feasible to estimate incremental impact; a customer ordering after a browse email does not prove they needed it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Rehearse data and suppression failures</h2>
      <p>Proposed fixtures: one accidental view, repeated duplicate events, a return visit, a collection reorganized after enrollment and a discontinued product. Verify the expected candidate and eligibility for each. Send a cart event and an order immediately before dispatch; expect the stale browse job to cancel.</p>
      <p>Also test missing permission, anonymous-to-known identity resolution, a shared-device mismatch and out-of-order delivery. Compare timestamps and cancellation logs rather than only inspecting a final segment count. No conversion result is claimed from these exercises.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Select, launch and maintain the workflow</h2>
      <p>Ask candidates to demonstrate supported view events, identity boundaries, candidate selection, dispatch rechecks, dynamic content fallbacks and exports. Verify the actual plan and integration rather than assuming any named app supports or lacks browse automation. Cost the realistic event, profile, send and maintenance volume on comparable terms.</p>
      <p>Roll out after the trigger contract and suppression fixtures pass. Keep a single dispatch owner, a pause action and a record of collection changes. Review enrollment quality after tracking or catalog changes. Reuse recent interest in launch or winback only within the stated permission and expiry rules; <a class="link" href="/use-cases/analytics">analytics</a> owns reproducible outcome reporting.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Browse abandonment FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
